{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2234978","formula":"C₂HNa₃O₆","hill":"C2HNa3O6","elements":["H","C","O","Na"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":1.0,"O":6.0,"Na":3.0},"names":{"en":"Sodium sesquicarbonate","ru":"Гидрокарбонат тринатрия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sodium sesquicarbonate (systematic name: trisodium hydrogendicarbonate) Na3H(CO3)2 is a double salt of sodium bicarbonate and sodium carbonate (NaHCO3 · Na2CO3), and has a needle-like crystal structure. However, the term is also applied to an equimolar mixture of those two salts, with whatever water of hydration the sodium carbonate includes, supplied as a powder. The dihydrate, Na3H(CO3)2 · 2H2O, occurs in nature as the evaporite mineral trona.","ru":"Гидрокарбона́т трина́трия (сесквикарбона́т на́трия, карбонат-гидрокарбонат натрия) — неорганическое соединение, кислая соль натрия и угольной кислоты с формулой Na3H(CO3)2, бесцветные игольчатые кристаллы, растворяется в воде, образует кристаллогидраты. Может рассматриваться как соединение карбоната и гидрокарбоната натрия: Na2(CO3)·NaH(CO3)."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":10791,"mass":189.99,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=O)(O)[O-].C(=O)([O-])[O-].[Na+].[Na+].[Na+]","inchikey":"WCTAGTRAWPDFQO-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"trisodium;hydrogen carbonate;carbonate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"10791","atoms":12,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.273,"y":-2.162,"z":-0.498,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.08,"y":-0.922,"z":-0.479,"el":"O"},{"x":0.88,"y":-2.812,"z":-0.561,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.325,"y":-2.839,"z":-0.469,"el":"O"},{"x":1.379,"y":-1.97,"z":-0.563,"el":"H"},{"x":0.247,"y":2.099,"z":0.712,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.036,"y":3.107,"z":1.41,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.753,"y":1.435,"z":0.016,"el":"O"},{"x":1.558,"y":1.651,"z":0.639,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.696,"y":-4.856,"z":-1.016,"el":"Na"